Day 40 – My First GitHub Actions Workflow 🚀

What I Learned

Today I created my first GitHub Actions workflow and understood how CI/CD works in practice.

Tasks Completed

- Created a new GitHub repository
- Created ".github/workflows/hello.yml"
- Triggered workflow on every push
- Used "actions/checkout@v4"
- Printed a Hello message
- Printed current date & time
- Printed branch name
- Listed repository files
- Printed runner operating system
- Broke the workflow intentionally ("exit 1") to understand pipeline failures
- Fixed the error and got my first ✅ Green Pipeline

Key Concepts Learned

- "on:" → When the workflow runs
- "jobs:" → Group of tasks
- "runs-on:" → Runner operating system
- "steps:" → Individual tasks
- "uses:" → Reusable GitHub Actions
- "run:" → Execute shell commands

Repository Structure

.github/
└── workflows/
    └── hello.yml

Today was the day CI/CD became real for me. Watching my first green pipeline run was an exciting milestone in my DevOps journey. 🚀

